        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "visionaries/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:visionaries:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "visionaries",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "visionaries",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Visionaries - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A visionary is not simply someone who was ahead of their time. They are someone who *identified a possibility space* — described what could exist before it existed — in a way that structured subsequent development. The best of them did this through specific, rigorous work: Turing's mathematical description of universal computation; Shannon's theorems about channel capacity; Wiener's cybernetics papers. The worst of them mistook speculation for prediction and produced frameworks that were intellectually stimulating but empirically wrong (Teilhard de Chardin's Omega Point; Kurzweil's singularity timeline)."
    },
